id: pm-review-release-gate
title: Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED
description: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:21:55.347Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T03:53:41.995Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:22:00.857Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:50:09.516Z",codex-agent,"CI previously executed the complete npm gate as individually listed steps. Consolidated those steps into npm run release:check so the required npm and Bun entrypoints are both exercised directly on the PR. Retained the explicit identity check and Bun graph-install check; no source thresholds or release checks were removed. Restoring the previous CI workflow makes the new entrypoint regression fail; restored check passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-25T23:52:19.919Z",codex-agent,"Pack verification: npm pack --dry-run --json and the actual npm pack --ignore-scripts artifact agree on 113 allowlisted files (dist: 108; root files: 5). Every packed member was scanned for absolute home paths, npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, private keys, hosted-data locations, private addresses and historical owner email addresses: PASS with zero matches. Regression proof: five independent workflow mutations (approval, provenance, token environment, daily schedule and OR bypass) plus the original manifest each fail the new contract check; restored contract passes 4/4. The linked test also passes through pm test --run --progress. Next gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-26T01:02:38.207Z",codex-agent,"Opening the release-readiness PR after package allowlist/privacy verification and focused regression proofs so complete npm and Bun CI can run in parallel with local full-gate verification. Pending checks are explicitly not treated as passing evidence. No timeout, threshold, dependency pin or test case is being relaxed."
  "2026-10-26T01:11:33.558Z",codex-agent,"Full local gates PASS: npm run release:check and bun run release:check, each with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Suite receipts: npm: 1/1/1/1/2/1/1/1/239/1 tests; bun: 1/1/1/1/2/1/1/1/239/1 tests. No thresholds were relaxed. The package remains unpublished and the approval variable unset; first publication requires the owner login and initial trusted-publisher registration. For the local first publish, explicitly override provenance with --provenance=false because publishConfig enables provenance for cloud CI. CI must confirm the final PR head. The tracker item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T00:10:57.608Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: preserve existing release-readiness work and merged main changes. Remove automatic release-workflow enablement; the orchestrator enables disabled schedules after merge. Require the canonical repository at job level for every write-permission or publishing job in the affected workflows, alongside the existing approval and branch conditions. Prove guard, approval, provenance and token regressions independently, then wait for complete npm and Bun CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T00:11:27.438Z",codex-agent,"Packed-artifact verification: 113 allowlisted files; dry-run and actual archive agree, and every packed member has zero private-data findings. Local project health passes with extensions disabled; globally installed extension version skew is outside this package."
  "2026-10-27T00:11:29.182Z",codex-agent,"Fork-exclusion revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts passes 6/6. Independently reverting each job repository guard, reverting all repository guards, allowing an OR bypass, removing approval or provenance, injecting a synthetic npm token environment, adding an unguarded CI write job, inheriting CI write permissions, adding a read-permission CI publisher, and restoring automatic setup all fail (each command exits nonzero; 12 independent mutations rejected). Restoring the workflows passes 6/6. Linked pm tests, test typecheck where present and lint pass. Canonical-repository checks include inherited permissions. Disabled release workflows remain for the orchestrator to enable after merge; no live settings or publishing were changed."
  "2026-10-27T01:53:52.958Z",codex-agent,"A newer main update landed while final CI was running. Integrate that upstream commit, preserving the release workflow and regression bytes exactly. Refresh pinned dependencies from the merged lockfile, rerun linked workflow checks, regenerate the changelog and scan the refreshed actual package before verifying complete npm and Bun CI on the new merge head. Existing independent revert proofs remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T01:54:11.687Z",codex-agent,"Main integration checks pass: linked workflow regressions, changelog currency, and the actual tarball allowlist/private-data scan (133 files, zero findings). Release workflow and approval regression source bytes are unchanged, including direct release-check entrypoint enforcement where applicable. The new main feature or toolchain update is retained; full npm and Bun CI must pass on the new merge head."
  "2026-10-27T03:17:46.670Z",codex-agent,"Independent re-review found the contract covered only release and CI files, missing CodeQL security-events writes, owner-only Dependabot guards and reusable workflow callers. Extend canonical-repository guards to every effectively write-enabled job in every workflow file. Replace regex workflow parsing with a pinned YAML parser, generic permission inheritance and negative fixtures for this full class. Correct local publishing documentation, preserve earlier readiness work, prove source reverts and wait for npm/Bun CI on every final head."
  "2026-10-27T03:53:39.368Z",codex-agent,"Whole-workflow contract passes 30/30 using the pinned YAML parser. It scans every YAML workflow, resolves aliases/flow maps, applies job permission overrides or workflow inheritance, and recognizes any scope with write plus write-all, including reusable callers. Negative fixtures cover CodeQL, owner-only/wrong-repository Dependabot, inherited writes, reusable calls, write-all, future scopes, missing publication approval/provenance, provenance overrides, token environments, OR/negation bypasses and discovery of a new workflow in a non-Git directory. Behavioural revert proof: all 14 independent mutations fail with assertion failures: each write job loses only its repository guard, owner-only/OR guards return, approval/provenance disappear, a synthetic token environment is added, file discovery is narrowed back to release/CI, permission matching returns to a scope allowlist, or inheritance is removed. Restoring the implementation passes 30/30. Linked pm tests and the repository's defined typecheck, lint and duplication checks pass. Maintainer local publishing is authenticated and checked, with no approval-variable hold; the variable gates automated GitHub releases."
